---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Contributing Sources">
  <div style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
      <h1 style="font-size: 2.25rem; font-weight: 800;">Contributing Data Sources</h1>
      <span class="badge" style="background-color: #dbeafe; color: #1e40af; font-size: 0.85rem;">
        Open Contribution Flow
      </span>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
      How community members and data providers add feeds to the Modafied independent benchmark.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem;">The 4-Step Onboarding Flow</h2>
    
    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem;">
      <div style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; background: var(--bg-subtle);">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          1. Open a Pull Request with One YAML File
        </h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          Create a single YAML configuration file under <code>catalog/sources/&lt;source-id&gt;.yaml</code> adhering to <code>schema/catalog/v0.2.json</code>.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
          Automated CI validates the schema, checks declared license fields, and performs a single probe fetch to verify endpoint connectivity and declarative record paths.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; background: var(--bg-subtle);">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          2. Automated 24-Hour Probation
        </h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          The probation runner snapshots the proposed feed on its declared cadence for 24 hours directly from the pull request branch.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
          A draft scorecard marked <code>probation</code> is posted as a PR comment to prove mechanical scoring works end-to-end.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; background: var(--bg-subtle);">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          3. License Verification
        </h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          Alex (designated CODEOWNER on <code>catalog/</code>) reviews the cited redistribution terms and license URL.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
          Nothing else is manual. We verify that redistribution is allowed under free, public terms.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem; background: var(--bg-subtle);">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          4. Merge and Baseline Publishing
        </h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          Once merged, the source is enrolled into the scheduled cron pipeline and published to the site.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
          All metric dimensions display <code>insufficient_data</code> until minimum sample thresholds (Rule H4) are satisfied. No fake numbers are ever published.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Minimal Source Adapter Template</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
      Each source requires declarative mapping for records, event timestamps, segmentation, and usage terms:
    </p>

    <pre><code>id: "example-feed"
name: "Example Weather Service"
description: "Public meteorological observation feed."
endpoints:
  - name: "current"
    url: "https://api.example.com/v1/current"
    method: "GET"
auth:
  type: "none"
license:
  spdx: "CC-BY-4.0"
  name: "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International"
  url: "https://example.com/legal/terms"
  redistribution_allowed: true
  attribution_required: true
  attribution_text: "Data provided by Example Weather Service"
refresh_cadence: "hourly"
records:
  path: "items"
  key: "station_id"
  event_time: "timestamp"
  event_time_format: "rfc3339"
segments:
  by: "region"
use_terms:
  commercial: "allowed"
  noncommercial: "allowed"
  attribution: "Example Weather Service"
  share_alike: false
  terms_url: "https://example.com/legal/terms"
fields:
  - name: "items[].temperature"
    type: "number"
  - name: "items[].humidity"
    type: "number"</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem; background-color: var(--bg-subtle);">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Core Constraints</h2>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
      <li><strong>No paid upstreams:</strong> All catalog feeds must have a free tier or be public domain.</li>
      <li><strong>No secrets in pull requests:</strong> If an endpoint requires an API key, specify the environment variable name in auth.env_var.</li>
      <li><strong>Contract-first:</strong> If a source structure cannot be expressed with existing fields, open an issue to extend the adapter schema first.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
